# HDVO END-USER LICENSE AGREEMENT (EULA) - ENGLISH TRANSLATION

All source code, documentation, configuration, validation data, and related files associated with HDVO (Human-in-the-Loop Hypothesis-Driven Validation and Optimization) distributed under the `tools/testing/hdvo/` and `harness/audit/hdvo/` directories, and their subdirectories (collectively, "HDVO Materials"), are the proprietary intellectual property and trade secrets of Nguyễn Lê Thiện Ân.

By using, copying, modifying, or executing these HDVO Materials, you agree to be bound by the terms of this License Agreement. If you do not agree, you are not authorized to use these materials.

## 1. Contribution-Based Limited License Grant
The Author hereby grants you a non-exclusive, non-transferable, non-sublicensable, worldwide, royalty-free license to use, execute, and modify the HDVO Materials **solely for the purpose of**:
* Personal, Educational, and Non-Commercial Evaluation of the SMap Core codebase.
* Developing, testing, semantically validating, and preparing code contributions (Pull Requests) directly to the official SMap repository at: `https://github.com/thienannguyen-cv/SMap`.

**Derivative Works of HDVO:** Any modifications, improvements, or derivative works based on the HDVO Materials themselves are subject to this EULA and may only be distributed via Pull Requests back to the official repository.

## 2. Prohibited Uses
Any use of the HDVO Materials outside the scope of Section 1 is strictly prohibited without the prior written consent of Nguyễn Lê Thiện Ân, including but not limited to:
* Using HDVO Materials to test, validate, or maintain independent forks, parallel derivative works, or any projects not intended for direct contribution to the official repository.
* Using HDVO Materials for mathematical models, algorithms, or applications outside of SMap Core.
* Integrating HDVO Materials into CI/CD pipelines or development/testing environments of any proprietary or commercial product or service.
* Selling, redistributing independently, leasing, or commercializing HDVO Materials in any form.

## 3. Legacy Development Alternative
HDVO is an optional tool designed to maintain semantic consistency. SMap Core remains fully open source under the Apache License 2.0. You may decline this EULA by not using the HDVO Materials, and continue to develop or contribute to SMap Core using traditional, legacy development and testing methods.

## 4. Disclaimer of Warranty & Limitation of Liability
The HDVO Materials are provided "AS IS", without warranty of any kind. In no event shall the Author be liable for any direct or indirect damages arising out of the use of these materials.

